# Dashboard and Team Management Rules

## Team Structure
- Teams are the primary organizational unit in the system
- Each team has:
  - Name
  - Description
  - Address
  - Contact information (phone, email)
  - Plan level (Enterprise, Business, Professional, Startup)
  - Associated employees

## Dashboard Components
- Dynamic team switcher in sidebar
- Real-time updates using PubSub
- Role-based access control
- Project list derived from teams

## State Management
- ETS table for dashboard state
- PubSub for real-time updates
- Component-specific state tracking
- Automatic state initialization

## Authorization Levels
- Basic users:
  - View teams
  - Access basic dashboard
  - View team projects
- Admin users:
  - Create/edit teams
  - Manage team members
  - Access admin dashboard
- Super Admin:
  - Full system access
  - Team management
  - System configuration

## Team-Project Relationship
- Projects are derived from teams
- Each team can have multiple projects
- Project data includes:
  - Team name
  - Team plan
  - Team URL
  - Associated icon

## Real-time Updates
- Team changes broadcast to subscribers
- Dashboard components update automatically
- State changes propagate through PubSub
- ETS table maintains current state

## Data Flow
1. Team changes trigger PubSub broadcast
2. Dashboard components receive updates
3. State updates stored in ETS
4. UI components refresh with new data

## Error Handling
- Graceful handling of empty teams
- Error recovery for ETS operations
- Fallback states for missing data
- Validation of team data

## Security
- Role-based access control
- Team-specific permissions
- Secure state management
- Protected team operations

## Best Practices
- Use PubSub for real-time updates
- Maintain consistent state
- Follow role-based access patterns
- Implement proper error handling
- Keep team data synchronized

## Implementation Guidelines
1. Initialize ETS table on startup
2. Subscribe to team updates
3. Handle state changes properly
4. Update UI components accordingly
5. Maintain data consistency

## Testing Requirements
- Test team creation/updates
- Verify real-time updates
- Check authorization levels
- Validate state management
- Test error scenarios

## Documentation
- Document team structure
- Explain state management
- Detail authorization rules
- Provide implementation examples
- Include error handling procedures
